PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_6classy_7_classy_5Class_20set_baseline, "\n        Set all input parameters to predefined baseline settings\n\n        This function offers an opportunity to quickly set all input parameters in one single line.\n\n        Currently, the possible predefined setting names are:\n\n        1. \047p18lb\047, or alternatively, any name containing \047planck\047, \04718\047, \047lens\047, and \047bao\047\n           Sets all parameters for computing the lensed and unlensed CMB l\047s and the matter power spectrum P(k) at z=0\n           (linear and non-linear with Halofit corrections)\n           for the best-fit model of the case \047Planck TTTEEE+lens + BAO\047 of the Planck 2018 papers.\n\n        2. \047p18l\047, or alternatively, any name containing \047planck\047, \04718\047, and \047lens\047\n           Sets all parameters for computing the lensed and unlensed CMB l\047s and the matter power spectrum P(k) at z=0\n           (linear and non-linear with Halofit corrections)\n           for the best-fit model of the case \047Planck TTTEEE+lens\047 of the Planck 2018 papers.\n\n        3. \047p18\047, or alternatively, any name containing \047planck\047 and \04718\047\n           Sets all parameters for computing the lensed and unlensed CMB l\047s and the matter power spectrum P(k) at z=0\n           (linear and non-linear with Halofit corrections)\n           for the best-fit model of the case \047Planck TTTEEE\047 of the Planck 2018 papers.\n\n        This choice of parameter settings is the same as in the baseline input files (input/baseline*.param)\n        of montepython [https://github.com/brinckmann/montepython_public] (see also 1210.7183, 1804.07261)\n\n        Parameters\n        ----------\n        baseline_name : str\n            Predefined setting name\n\n        Returns\n        -------\n        None\n        ");
