PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_6classy_7_classy_5Class_114get_transfer, "\n        Return all scalar transfer functions at z\n\n        Return a dictionary of transfer functions at all wavenumbers\n        for scalar perturbations and at redshift z.  The name and list\n        of quantities in the returned dictionary are defined in CLASS,\n        in perturbations_output_titles() and\n        perturbations_output_data(), using either the \047class\047 format\n        (default) or \047camb\047 format. The keys of the dictionary refer\n        to wavenumbers \047k (h/Mpc)\047, and in \047class\047 format, to density\n        fluctuations \047d_g\047, etc., velocity perturbations \047t_g\047, etc.,\n        and metric perturbations. In \047camb\047 format, besides\n        wavenumbers \047k (h/Mpc)\047, the returned transfer functions are\n        \047-T_g/k2\047, etc.  For each key, the dictionary contains an\n        array of values corresponding to each sampled value of\n        wavenumber.\n\n        This function works if \047output\047 contains at least \047mTk\047 for\n        density transfer function and/or \047vTk\047 for velocity transfer\n        functions. To get the transfer functions at some z>0, the user\n        must set \047z_pk\047 or \047z_max_pk\047 to a value equal or bigger to\n        the requested one.\n\n        Parameters\n        ----------\n        z : float, optional\n            Redshift (0 by default)\n\n        output_format : str, optional\n            Output format, one of \047class\047 (defualt) or \047camb\047\n\n        Returns\n        -------\n        transfers : dict\n            Dictionary of all transfer functions at each wavenumber\n        ");
