PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_6classy_7_classy_5Class_138get_sources, "\n        Return the source functions stored in the perturbation module at all sampled (k, tau)\n\n        After integrating all perturbations (more precisely, all\n        transfer functions) over time, the CLASS perturbation module\n        stores a list of the most important combinations of them on a\n        grid of (k,tau) values. This includes the combinations used\n        later to compute the CMB and LSS observables. This function\n        retrieves these source functions directly from the CLASS\n        structure \047perturbations\047, and returns them together with the\n        values of k and tau at which they are sampled.\n\n        The output is a dictionary whose keys belong to the list:\n        -\047p\047 for the CMB polarization source\n        -\047phi\047 for the metric fluctuation phi of the Newtonian gauge\n        -\047phi_plus_psi\047 for the metric fluctuation phi+psi of the Newtonian gauge\n        -\047phi_prime\047 for the metric fluctuation phi\047 of the Newtonian gauge\n        -\047psi\047 for the metric fluctuation psi of the Newtonian gauge\n        -\047H_T_Nb_prime\047 for the metric fluctuation H_T\047 of the Nboisson gauge\n        -\047k2gamma_Nb\047 for the k^2 gamma of the Nboisson gauge\n        -\047h\047 for the metric fluctuation h of the synchronouys gauge\n        -\047h_prime\047  for the metric fluctuation h\047 of the synchronouys gauge\n        -\047eta\047 for the metric fluctuation eta of the synchronouys gauge\n        -\047eta_prime\047  for the metric fluctuation eta\047 of the synchronouys gauge\n        -\047delta_tot\047  for the total density fluctuation\n        -\047delta_m\047 for the non-relativistic density fluctuation\n        -\047delta_cb\047 for the CDM+baryon density fluctuation\n        -\047delta_g\047 for the photon density fluctuation\n        -\047delta_b\047 for the baryon density fluctuation\n        -\047delta_cdm\047 for the CDM density fluctuation\n        -\047delta_idm\047 for the inter""acting DM density fluctuation\n        -\047delta_dcdm\047 for the decaying DM density fluctuation\n        -\047delta_fld\047 for the fluid density fluctuation\n        -\047delta_scf\047 for the scalar field density fluctuation\n        -\047delta_dr\047 for the decay radiation density fluctuation\n        -\047delta_ur\047 for the ultra-relativistic density fluctuation\n        -\047delta_idr\047 for the interacting dark radiation density fluctuation\n        -\047delta_ncdm[i]\047 for the ncdm[i] density fluctuation\n        -\047theta_tot\047 for the total velocity divergence\n        -\047theta_m\047 for the non-relativistic velocity divergence\n        -\047theta_cb\047 for the CDM+baryon velocity divergence\n        -\047theta_g\047 for the photon velocity divergence\n        -\047theta_b\047 for the baryon velocity divergence\n        -\047theta_cdm\047 for the CDM velocity divergence\n        -\047theta_idm\047 for the interacting DM velocity divergence\n        -\047theta_dcdm\047 for the decaying DM velocity divergence\n        -\047theta_fld\047 for the fluid velocity divergence\n        -\047theta_scf\047 for the scalar field velocity divergence\n        -\047theta_dr\047 for the decayt radiation velocity divergence\n        -\047theta_ur\047 for the ultra-relativistic velocity divergence\n        -\047theta_ncdm[i]\047 for the ncdm[i] velocity divergence\n\n        The list of actual keys in the returned dictionary depends on\n        what the user requested in the \047output\047 field.\n\n        For each key, the returned dictionary contains an array of sources, indexed as:\n\n        sources[\047key\047][index_k][index_tau]\n\n        Parameters\n        ----------\n        None\n\n        Returns\n        -------\n        sources : dict\n            Dictionary containing the source functions sources[\047key\047][index_k][index_tau] (dimensionless)\n        numpy array : k_array\n            Array of k values (units of 1/Mpc)\n        numpy array :"" tau_array\n            Array of tau values (units of Mpc)\n        ");
