PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_6classy_7_classy_5Class_144get_qcdm_fast_b0_tree, "\n        Evaluate the deterministic exact-time c-c\047 tree-level bispectrum monopole.\n\n        This is the bulk triangle analogue of ``get_qcdm_fast_pkpoles``.  It\n        reuses the exact-QS cosmology/kernel cache created by the most recent\n        ``nonlinear_pt_init`` call and evaluates\n\n          B = 2 Z1(k1) Z1(k2) Z2(k1,k2) P1 P2 + 2 cyclic\n\n        followed by the full line-of-sight monopole average.  The C routine\n        applies the same DESI AP convention as the fast power-spectrum path and,\n        when enabled in CLASS, the leading anisotropic tree-level IR damping.\n        If ``sigma_B>0`` it additionally applies the DESI DR1 bispectrum FoG\n        factor inside the orientation integral.  ``sigma_B=0`` is exactly the\n        previously validated tree-level path.\n\n        Parameters\n        ----------\n        k1_h, k2_h, k3_h : array_like\n            Equal-length one-dimensional arrays of observed/fiducial triangle\n            sides in h/Mpc.  Each row must satisfy the triangle inequalities.\n        z : float\n            Must be one of the z_pk values used in the CLASS computation.\n        params : mapping or length-24 array_like\n            Same native tracer vector as ``get_qcdm_fast_pkpoles``.  The current\n            deterministic B0 core ignores power-spectrum-only counterterm and\n            stochastic entries, but they remain in the vector so both APIs have\n            an identical nuisance-state convention.  Primordial fNL entries\n            must currently be zero.\n        nmu, nphi : int, optional\n            Orientation quadrature sizes.  Passing 0 lets nonlinear_pt.c choose\n            its cached/default values (with a minimum of 12 in each direction).\n            Positive values must be >= 2.\n        sigma_B : float, optional\n            DESI bispectrum FoG scale in Mpc/h.  Must be finite and non-negative.\n            The default 0 recovers the validated undamped tree B0 exactly.\n        hratio, Dratio : ""float, optional\n            External AP ratios with ``hratio=H_true/H_fid=1/q_parallel`` and\n            ``Dratio=D_M,true/D_M,fid=q_perp``.  Supply both or neither.\n\n        Returns\n        -------\n        ndarray, shape (ntri,)\n            Deterministic tree-level B0 in (Mpc/h)^6.\n        ");
